  "text_sanskrit": "भूतग्रामः स एवायं भूत्वा भूत्वा प्रलीयते । रात्र्यागमेऽवशः पार्थ प्रभवत्यहरागमे ॥ ८-१९ ॥",
  "itrans": "bhUtagrAmaH sa evAyaM bhUtvA bhUtvA pralIyate . rAtryAgame.avashaH pArtha prabhavatyaharAgame .. 8-19 ..",
  "translation": "The same multitude of beings, (as we observe), is born again and again, and at the coming of night, under the power of the Lord, goes to dissolution, O Partha; and it is again originated at the coming of day. (19)\nA. When Brahman's day and night are spoken of, one might mistake that the Lord also has a beginning and an end. This is refuted in the next two verses.",
